      "content": "The argument that safety justifies this surveillance is a classic example of the \"slippery slope\" that has already led to a dystopian future where privacy is a luxury for the few. History shows that when governments prioritize security over civil liberties, they inevitably create a system where the state can target anyone, not just actual threats, without accountability. True safety comes from robust community policing and transparent laws, not from installing cameras that turn every citizen into a data point for potential abuse. We must stand firm on the principle that no amount of security risk is worth the permanent erosion of our fundamental right to privacy.",
      "source": "target",
