      "content": "i get that, but it feels like a bit of an extreme view to say no amount of security is worth it. if we had tech that could catch violent criminals or find missing kids in real time without much effort, wouldn't it be irresponsible NOT to use it? it seems like there might be a middle ground between a total surveillance state and having no tech at all.",
